Atlas overlay patch 0101: ui/kit-app-menu
Why: with the Kit chrome on, the app menu is a Kit popover (chrome/browser/ui/atlas/kit/kit_app_menu.cc):
the engine's AppMenuModel stays the source of the entries, their enabled state, checks and shortcuts, the
Kit draws them (rows of 28, radius 12, accent row, section separators, submenus as a popover with a back row).
One call at the top of BrowserAppMenuButton::ShowMenuWithFlags; it returns false (the engine's own menu is
shown) unless the browser starts with --atlas-kit-chrome.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/views/toolbar/browser_app_menu_button.cc
Test filter: *AtlasKit*
Rebase risk: L (one include, one call in a function that has not changed shape for years)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

